# Create work order in Marketplace (testing)

Use this rule when you need a **real work order** in the **Marketplace (MP) testing** environment so local runs (RabbitMQ, Roo, DB checks) use **consistent WO data** you control.

## What “create a work order” means (default)

When the user asks to **create a work order** (or similar: “new WO in MP”, “Marketplace work order”, etc.) **without** saying they only want the form or submit, treat the task as **complete Marketplace setup for ResiRoo**, not “stop after **SUBMIT WORK ORDER**”:

1. **Create:** Fill and submit the new-WO form (client, location, **issue description**, title, etc.) per the steps below.
2. **Triage:** On the post-submit **`request-id=`** page, **wait** until **Work Order Triage** has **finished** (stable UI, not stuck in “Doing Triage…” / loading).
3. **Resiroo:** Open the work order **⋮** menu and run **Start Resiroo Manually**, then **verify** the action actually ran (see **Verify Start Resiroo Manually** below — clicking the label alone is **not** proof). **Then close the ⋮ menu** by clicking **outside** the dropdown on **WO panel content** (see **After submit: … Steps** — do **not** use **Details** or top-bar controls like **Search Jobs** to dismiss).
4. **Ids:** Obtain a **Bearer JWT** for the Marketplace API (see **API auth — capture JWT**). Prefer **`GET …/api/WorkOrder/{jobToken}`** where **`jobToken`** is the **`request-id=`** UUID from the WO URL (same pattern as **MPHelper** / `vtools.user.js` — direct fetch by job token). From that JSON, read **`workOrderId`**, **`woNumber`**, **`clientId`**, resident id under **`aiResidentComData`**, etc. If that endpoint or shape fails for your build, fall back to **`GET …/api/Job/List/{jobToken}`** → numeric **`workOrderId`**, then **`GET …/api/WorkOrder/ById/{workOrderId}`**. Use the **API base** from **`.env.e2e.local`** (or derived from **`MARKETPLACE_URL`**).

**Only skip triage wait and/or Start Resiroo** if the user **explicitly** asks for a partial flow (e.g. “create but do not start Resiroo”, “submit only”).

## Agent responsibility (when this rule applies)

- **Create the work order in Marketplace through its web app** — not via a substitute script or invented API **unless** the user explicitly chooses another method **or** **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-work-order.mdc`** is in scope (that rule documents the verified **`POST …/api/WorkOrder`** multipart API path for fast testing).
- **Do the full UI path:** load **`MARKETPLACE_URL`** and credentials from **`.env.e2e.local`**, **open MP**, **log in**, then **create a new work order** whose title, **issue description**, priority/labels, category, and resident/location match the **scenario the user gave** (e.g. weather-related, emergency, plumbing). The **issue description** field on the form is **required** — **do not** submit until it is filled with a clear maintenance/issue narrative (see step 8 below).
- Use the **browser automation tools** available in Cursor when you can (navigate, snapshot, fill forms). If login is blocked (CAPTCHA, SSO, unknown selector, missing permission to `source` the env file), **stop**, say what failed, and ask the user to complete that step or provide a session.
- **Do not** claim the job is done after submit alone when the user asked to **create a work order** in the default sense — see **What “create a work order” means** above. **Do not** claim the WO is fully ready for ResiRoo testing until **Start Resiroo Manually** has been **verified** per **Verify Start Resiroo Manually** (unless the user opted out of Resiroo).
- **Do not** claim the WO exists until the UI flow has finished and you have a real id (or the user confirms creation).
- After submit, follow **Work Order Triage → Start Resiroo Manually → verify `ForceResiroo` POST 200** (see below), **then close the ⋮ menu**, **then** pull **`workOrderId`**, **resident user id** (correct JSON paths — see below), **`clientId`**, etc. from the **Marketplace API** — do not skip triage wait or the verified manual Resiroo start for a default “create work order” request. **Do not** use top-level **`data.userId`** as the resident id unless you have verified it matches the resident (it often does not — see **Staff vs resident user**).

## Required chat response (final reply to the user)

When this rule applies and you created a work order (default flow), the **final message back to the user** must include a **structured work-order summary** so they can copy values into RabbitMQ payloads, DB checks, and tickets **without** re-running discovery.

**Always include (when known from UI + API):**

| Field | Source | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|
| **Marketplace UI URL** | Browser | Testing vs dev/prod; no secrets. |
| **WO title** | Create form / WO header | As shown in MP. |
| **Job token** | URL `request-id=` | UUID; **not** the numeric work order id. |
| **Work order id** (`workOrderId` / `ObjectId`) | Prefer **`GET …/api/WorkOrder/{jobToken}`** (UUID from `request-id=`) → `data.workOrderId` if present, else **`data.jobs[0].workOrderId`** (and variants). Else **`GET …/api/Job/List/{jobToken}`** → `data[].workOrderId`. | Numeric id for **`AdditionalData.WorkOrderId`**. **MPHelper** uses the **`/api/WorkOrder/{uuid}`** path with the URL job token. |
| **`woNumber`** | **`WorkOrder/{jobToken}`** or **`ById`** → `data.woNumber` | May be `null` briefly; retry. |
| **`clientId`** | **`WorkOrder/{jobToken}`** or **`ById`** → `data.clientId` | Compare to **`CLIENT_ID`** in **`.env.e2e.local`** if present. |
| **Resident user id** | Same JSON → `data.aiResidentComData.resident.userId` or `data.location.locationAssignments[0].userId` | For **`ResidentUserId`**; **not** top-level `data.userId`. |
| **Staff / creator user id** (optional) | **`ById`** → `data.userId` | Label as staff/creator; do **not** substitute for resident. |
| **Location** | **`ById`** / UI | Address or name as relevant for the test. |
| **API base used** | **`.env.e2e.local`** (`VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL` if set) or derived from **`MARKETPLACE_URL`** | Must align with **`MARKETPLACE_URL`** (e.g. testing MP → `https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai`). |

Use a **small table or bullet list** in the reply (markdown is fine). **Do not** paste **JWTs**, **bearer tokens**, or passwords.

**If API resolution fails** (e.g. **`401`/`403`** on **`WorkOrder/{jobToken}`**, **`Job/List`**, or **`WorkOrder/ById`**, timeout, missing token):

- Still report everything you **know from the UI**: **job token**, **title**, **client name**, **location label/address**, and the **exact API base** you attempted.
- Say clearly which fields are **not** available yet (**work order id**, **resident user id**, **`clientId`**, **`woNumber`**). Retry with a **Bearer captured from DevTools → Network** on any **`api-*-marketplace.vendoroo.ai`** request (see **API auth — capture JWT**), then retry **`GET …/api/WorkOrder/{jobToken}`** before falling back to **`Job/List`** — **do not invent UUIDs or numeric ids**.
- Optionally give the **exact GET paths** (no bearer) so the user can run them after fixing auth.

**Task is not “complete” for copy-paste test use** until **`workOrderId`**, **`clientId`**, and **resident user id** are resolved **or** the user accepts the blocked-API handoff above.

## Terms

- **MP** — Marketplace (Vendoroo work-order product UI + APIs).
- **WO** / **wo** — work order.

